hich include the earliest monumental hieroglyphs dating back around 5,200 years. These new inscriptions were not previously recorded by any expedition and are of great significance in the history of the ancient Egyptian writing systems, according to Egyptologist John Coleman Darnell, professor in Yale\'s Department of Near Eastern Languages and Civilizations at Yale, who co-directs the Elkab Desert Survey Project."'}], {'usage.total_tokens': 922, 'usage.prompt_tokens': 843})
